// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//
// Operator gate: softmax. `[2026-08-09]` The operator corrected `runlist`
// needs, so that its attention interior can run on the device with nothing on
// the host.
//
// Row-wise softmax over the STREAMING family in
// programming_examples/softmax/softmax.cc -- init_softmax_scale_buffer, one
// partial_softmax_rows_bf16 over the whole row, normalize_softmax_rows_bf16.
// Not the single-shot softmax_bf16 in the same file, which subtracts no row
// max and fixes the row width at 256; the streaming family does subtract a
// running max and takes row_width and num_rows as runtime int32. No kernel was
// written for this: the object was already built by compile_kernels.py and no
// builder had ever linked it.
//
// Three shapes, and the third is the reason the operator exists. 512x512 is
// the bring-up point and 4096x768 the block's own activation shape; 64x4096 is
// ATTENTION width, because a per-head score matrix is [seq, seq] and the row
// width is therefore the sequence length rather than the hidden size. It is
// also where the builder's L1 budget bites -- three [rows_per_call, cols] bf16
// buffers live in L1, so rows_per_call drops 8 -> 2 at that width.
//
// Runs opcheck.py on real NPU2 against an FP32 reference: np.isclose over the
// full output at rtol=1.6e-2, zero permitted mismatches, PLUS a mean_rel_L1
// ceiling. The ceiling is not decoration. A softmax row spans three orders of
// magnitude, so an atol sized the registry way -- from the worst element -- is
// set by the few large outputs and is loose against the small ones; the
// aggregate bound is what an element-wise check cannot express. See
// opcheck_specs.py for both numbers and how they were measured.
//
// NPU serialization lives one layer down, not in the recipes below. Device
// access is locked on /tmp/npu.lock, which XRTRunner.run_test holds across
// xclbin load and dispatch -- the same inode lit.cfg.py's NPU substitution and
// KernelCache take. Taking the outer /tmp/mlir-air-npu.lock here would
// DEADLOCK against the gate command that already holds it, since BSD flock(2)
// treats a second open() of the same file as a foreign lock.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for its directives, so naming
// one in prose -- even inside a comment -- registers as a second directive and
// leaves the test UNRESOLVED. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_softmax_peano
// RUN: cd test_npu2_softmax_peano
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-softmax PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// Both lines per shape, not just the verdict: the first is XRTRunner's own,
// the second names the operator and shape, so a test wired to the wrong
// operator fails here rather than passing quietly.
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] softmax [512x512]: PASS
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] softmax [4096x768]: PASS
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] softmax [64x4096]: PASS
//
// THE NEGATIVE CONTROL, WHICH THIS OPERATOR NEEDED MORE THAN MOST.
//
// It is a separate arm rather than a shared one because softmax's injection
// target is chosen per shape BY MEASUREMENT, and that choice is load-bearing.
// Every other row-wise operator here injects at (rows-1, 0). For softmax that
// position does not discriminate: +2.0 on a low-probability element moves the
// whole tensor by 1.06e-3 at 512x512 and 7.43e-3 at 4096x768, against an atol
// of 7.5e-3, so the injected run PASSED -- measured, not hypothesised, on the
// first version of these rows. At 512x512 the injected run's abs_err_max
// equalled the clean run's exactly, so no atol admitting the clean run could
// have rejected it; the target had to move, not the tolerance.
//
// prepare_softmax now perturbs the LAST ROW'S ARGMAX, which moves the tensor
// 12-18x over atol at all three shapes. What that buys: a control that fails
// here is saying the comparison resolves a single ELEMENT of a single ROW out
// of the whole tensor, because softmax is row-independent and everything
// outside that row must stay exact.
//
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-softmax-fault PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FAULT
//
// The injected element first, so an injection that silently perturbed nothing
// is visible here rather than read backwards from the verdict. The column is
// the measured argmax and differs per shape, so it is matched loosely; the ROW
// is pinned, because "the last row" is the part of the choice that is not
// data-dependent.
// FAULT: [fault-inject] input 0 at (511, {{[0-9]+}})
// FAULT: [opcheck] softmax [512x512]: FAIL
// FAULT: [opcheck] softmax [512x512]: fault-inject input -> FAIL (as required)
// FAULT: [fault-inject] input 0 at (4095, {{[0-9]+}})
// FAULT: [opcheck] softmax [4096x768]: FAIL
// FAULT: [opcheck] softmax [4096x768]: fault-inject input -> FAIL (as required)
// FAULT: [fault-inject] input 0 at (63, {{[0-9]+}})
// FAULT: [opcheck] softmax [64x4096]: FAIL
// FAULT: [opcheck] softmax [64x4096]: fault-inject input -> FAIL (as required)
// FAULT: NEGATIVE CONTROL: PASS
